comments.body:
Thank you for that context @participant4 :<nick>:. This makes it clear what happens now:

(1) `skimage` cannot be assumed to be compatible with `dask` arrays without additional work, and therefore we shall not test against it;
(2) `skimage` will continue our work on allowing dispatching via `spatch`, and this may enable benefiting from dask via `dask-image` or other backend implementations;
(2) `api-array-compat` may want to make some changes to make their dask namespace's behavior less surprising. From @participant3's comment above it's not 100% clear whether they'd want to do that, but my hunch is that it's necessary.

Thanks all for your input! I consider this issue resolved from the skimage perspective.
